/**
\defgroup editor CoreEditor
\brief In-game editor tools drawn with Dear ImGui: the Entity Debugger, the FPS Counter, a sprite-sheet viewer, and any tool windows you write, including game UI.

<table class="markdownTable">
<tr><td><b>Source</b></td><td>\srcdir{include/Editor} · \srcdir{src/Editor}</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Include</b></td><td>`#include <Editor/Module.hpp>` (tools, `Open`) · `#include <Editor/DebugStatsEditor.hpp>`, `<Editor/EntityEditorTool.hpp>`, `<Editor/SpriteSheetEditor.hpp>` (built-in tools)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Namespaces</b></td><td>`CoreEditor`; the tool base class is ImGUIWrapper::IEditorTool</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Started by</b></td><td>\srclink{src/Module.cpp,89,Engine::InitializePlugins()}, last</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Examples</b></td><td>\ref ex_editor · the HUD in every game</td></tr>
</table>

## How to use

An **editor tool** is a class derived from ImGUIWrapper::IEditorTool with a `Draw_Internal()` function full of ImGui calls. Every frame, between `ImGui::NewFrame()` and rendering, the engine calls `Draw_Internal()` on each open tool (\src{src/Editor/Module.cpp,41,51}). That makes tools the place for debug windows **and** for game UI such as a score display.

<b>1. Write the tool:</b>

\genexopen{modules/EditorTools.cpp,A tool with buttons\, sliders and a colour picker}
\snippet modules/EditorTools.cpp tool
\endex

<b>2. Open it</b> once, after Engine::InitializePlugins(). CoreEditor::Open<T>() creates the tool the first time and returns the same instance on later calls:

\genexopen{modules/EditorTools.cpp,Open}
\snippet modules/EditorTools.cpp open
\endex

<b>3. Close and reopen it</b> from game code with `Close()` and `Open()`; a closed tool keeps its state. Passing `&bOpen` to `ImGui::Begin` gives the window a close button that does the same:

\genexopen{modules/EditorTools.cpp,Toggling a tool with a key}
\snippet modules/EditorTools.cpp toggle
\endex

Override `OnOpenStateChanged(bool)` to react when a tool opens or closes.

## Built-in tools

| Tool | Opens | Shows |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Entity Debugger** (CoreEditor::EntityEditorTool) | At startup | Create entities; *Entity Outliner* lists entities that have an `FTransformComponent`, click one to select it; the selected entity's components with editable fields; *Add Component* for any registered component; *Save Entity* writes it as a flecs script to `Resources/Output/ECS/<name>`; *Global Entity* shows ECS::GetGlobalSystemsEntity() (\src{src/Editor/EntityEditorTool.cpp,223,243}) |
| **FPS Counter** (CoreEditor::DebugStatsEditor) | At startup | Frame rate and frame time (\src{src/Editor/DebugStatsEditor.cpp,11,19}) |
| **Sprite Sheet** (CoreEditor::SpriteSheetEditor) | From a sprite's *Open Sprite Sheet* button | A zoomable view of the sprite's texture with a grid |
| **Dear ImGui Demo** | Always (\src{src/Editor/Module.cpp,44}) | ImGui's own demo; collapse it with ▼ |

Component panels in the Entity Debugger:

- `FTransformComponent` has a move gizmo drawn over the game: drag it to move the entity (\src{src/Editor/EntityEditorTool.cpp,61,80}).
- `FTexture2DComponent` has a texture drop-down, its UV fields, *Open Sprite Sheet*, and *Update* (\src{src/Editor/EntityEditorTool.cpp,82,107}).
- Your own components get a panel from the `DEFINE_COMPONENT` macros (\ref ecs_components).

Reopen a built-in tool you closed with `CoreEditor::Open<CoreEditor::DebugStatsEditor>()` (or `EntityEditorTool`).

## Game UI with tools

The examples' HUDs are tools that draw a small window with no title bar and no input, anchored to a corner of the game window. They also collapse the ImGui demo window once:

\genexopen{games/Dodge.cpp,The Dodge HUD}
\snippet games/Dodge.cpp hud
\endex

## Things to watch out for

- Tools are drawn outside the ECS update, so entity changes made in `Draw_Internal()` happen immediately. Wrap loops that create or destroy entities in `ECS::GetWorld().defer(...)`.
- `CoreEditor::Open<T>()` keeps one instance per tool type; you cannot open two windows of the same tool class.
- Tools are never destroyed or unregistered; closing only hides them.
- With multi-viewport on, place windows relative to `ImGui::GetMainViewport()->Pos`; see \ref imguiwrapper.
- The Entity Debugger's component headers cannot be collapsed (\src{include/Gameplay/ECS/Components.hpp,43}).
*/

